 "internal_silences": [],
 "text": "Every month, I spend one day walking in the hills near my town. I leave early, before the paths become busy. I pack water, a sandwich and a warm jacket, even in summer. The weather in the hills can change very quickly. I follow marked paths and carry a paper map as well as my phone. Walking for several hours clears my head in a way nothing else can. I come home tired, but with a clear head. If you have never tried it, start with a short route. Choose a clear day, and tell someone where you are going. The hills will always be there, ready for your next walk and your next view."
